  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/window-object.html#the-windowproxy-exotic-object says\r\n\r\n> As long as the [`Window`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/window-object.html#window) object remains an ordinary object this [i.e., `WindowProxy`] is unobservable and can be implemented either way.\r\n\r\nBut `Window` objects are not ordinary objects, since they allow [named property access](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/window-object.html#named-access-on-the-window-object) through a Web IDL getter which automatically makes them [legacy platform objects](https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#es-legacy-platform-objects), a kind of exotic object.\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nWithout this being one of the reasons for the existence of `WindowProxy`, I wonder what the purpose `WindowProxy` still serves. I know currently it is also used for indexed access of children frames but that can reasonably be implemented on `Window` instead. ",
